            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "maanug-nv"
            },
            "body": "Hi @WoosungMyung . So sorry for the lack of response on this PR. \r\nJust fyi, we are planning to deprecate parallel state in the future in favor of a more flexible solution that works better with multimodal and encoder-decoder models. But I think this can still be merged for now, while that refactor is still happening.\r\n\r\nI think it would be good to add some unit tests for these functions, would you be able to add those?\r\n\r\nAlso, since you mentioned the intent is to make this config info available in W&B, I wanted to note that you can already find the config details in W&B in the 'Overview' tab in the 'Config' section:\r\n<img width=\"1224\" height=\"510\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ede9b33-1780-495b-9ac8-1b0d8c8fd930\" />\r\n\r\nThe entire config including parallelism sizes are also dumped in the log file. If that works for your needs, then feel free to close the PR. Otherwise, please kindly add unit tests for these functions and then we can get this reviewed and merged.",
